findings.fix:
Add an alias definition to `vite.config.ts` (or create one) or change the imports to relative paths. Example fix:
```ts
// vite.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';
import { fileURLToPath, URL } from 'node:url';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      '@': fileURLToPath(new URL('./src', import.meta.url))
    }
  }
});
```
Or update the imports in `src/App.tsx` to use relative paths, e.g., `import Layout from "./components/Layout";`.
